"donor_test":"not tested","donor_padj":null,"donor_log2fc":null,"donor_lfcse":null,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":null},{"cell_type":"OPC","gene_symbol":"PRPF4B","gene_symbol_current":"PRP4K","gene_id":"ENSG00000112739","nucleus_tested":true,"nucleus_significant":false,"nucleus_direction":"higher in AD","nucleus_padj":0.891713,"nucleus_log2fc":0.0613028,"nucleus_score":0.338778,"pct_ad":0.172684,"pct_control":0.168582,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.984213,"donor_log2fc":0.189576,"donor_lfcse":0.176173,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":0.00124464},{"cell_type":"Oli","gene_symbol":"PRPF4B","gene_symbol_current":"PRP4K","gene_id":"ENSG00000112739","nucleus_tested":true,"nucleus_significant":true,"nucleus_direction":"higher in AD","nucleus_padj":0.000706954,"nucleus_log2fc":0.211432,"nucleus_score":3.77742,"pct_ad":0.130616,"pct_control":0.111135,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.902484,"donor_log2fc":0.0991571,"donor_lfcse":0.139582,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":0.00477961}],"modules":[{"cell_type":"Ast","gene_id":"ENSG00000112739","module":"magenta","kme":0.151494,"hub":false,"module_direction":"higher in AD","module_padj":0.656828,"module_significant":false}],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000112739","entrez_id":["8899"],"uniprot":["Q13523"],"ncbi_summary":"Pre-mRNA splicing occurs in two sequential transesterification steps, and the protein encoded by this gene is thought to be involved in pre-mRNA splicing and in signal transduction. This protein belongs to a kinase family that includes serine/arginine-rich protein-specific kinases and cyclin-dependent kinases (CDKs). This protein is regarded as a CDK-like kinase (Clk) with homology to mitogen-activated protein kinases (MAPKs). [provided by RefSeq, Jul 2008].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q13523","text":"Serine/threonine kinase involved in spliceosomal assembly as well as mitosis and signaling regulation (PubMed:10799319, PubMed:12077342, PubMed:17513757, PubMed:17998396). Connects chromatin mediated regulation of transcription and pre-mRNA splicing (PubMed:12077342). During spliceosomal assembly, interacts with and phosphorylates PRPF6 and PRPF31, components of the U4/U6-U5 tri-small nuclear ribonucleoprotein (snRNP), to facilitate the formation of the spliceosome B complex. Plays a role in regulating transcription and the spindle assembly checkpoint (SAC) (PubMed:20118938). Associates with U5 snRNP and NCOR1 deacetylase complexes which may allow a coordination of pre-mRNA splicing with chromatin remodeling events involved in transcriptional regulation (PubMed:12077342). Associates and probably phosphorylates SMARCA4 and NCOR1 (PubMed:12077342). Phosphorylates SRSF1 (PubMed:11418604). Associates with kinetochores during mitosis and is necessary for recruitment and maintenance of the checkpoint proteins such as MAD1L1 and MAD12L1 at the kinetochores (PubMed:17998396). Phosphorylates and regulates the activity of the transcription factors such as ELK1 and KLF13 (PubMed:10799319, PubMed:17513757). Phosphorylates nuclear YAP1 and WWTR1/TAZ which induces nuclear exclusion and regulates Hippo signaling pathway, involved in tissue growth control (PubMed:29695716)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_03","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}